  "body": "## Finding Description\n\nIn the function `L2TokenReceiverV2::increaseLiquidityCurrentRange`, the protocol currently uses `block.timestamp` as the `deadline` argument when interacting with the Uniswap Nonfungible Position Manager. This effectively **defeats the purpose of the deadline parameter**.\n\nUsing `block.timestamp` as the deadline has no protective effect because the timestamp corresponds to the moment the transaction is mined. As a result, the deadline check compares `block.timestamp` against the same value, rendering it a no-op.\n\n> Note: A similar issue was assessed as **medium severity** in a recent [Code4rena contest](https://code4rena.com/reports/2024-03-revert-lend#m-21-dangerous-use-of-deadline-parameter).\n## Impact\n\nWithout a proper deadline, pending transactions can be executed maliciously at a later time. For example:\n\n- Transactions with insufficient gas may not be mined immediately.\n- Malicious actors or MEV bots could execute these delayed transactions at a disadvantage to the original submitter.\n\nThis issue has been discussed in depth in [this reference](https://github.com/code-423n4/2022-12-backed-findings/issues/64).\n## Recommended Mitigation\n\nTo mitigate this risk:\n\n1. Add a `deadline` parameter to `L2TokenReceiverV2::increaseLiquidityCurrentRange`.\n2. Forward this parameter to the corresponding call in the Uniswap Nonfungible Position Manager.\n\nThis approach is already applied correctly in `L2TokenReceiverV2::swap` and `L1SenderV2::swapExactInputMultihop`.",
  "proof_of_concept": "Please note this POC is via foundry. It shows that increasing the liquidity is always executed at `block.timestamp`, even after a vm.warp. \n\nTo setup foundry in the project, execute the following commands \n\n```\nforge init . --force\nforge install openzeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts\nforge build\n```\n\nin `foundry.toml`, add the following line \n\n`test = 'testFoundry'`\n\nIn the root of the project, create a new folder called `2025-08-morpheus/testFoundry` and add the following test into a file named `L2TokenReceiverV2.t.sol`, and run the following command `forge test --mt test_increaseLiquidityCurrentRange_usesBlockTimestampAsDeadline`\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.20;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {L2TokenReceiverV2} from \"../contracts/capital-protocol/L2TokenReceiverV2.sol\";\nimport {INonfungiblePositionManager} from \"../contracts/interfaces/uniswap-v3/INonfungiblePositionManager.sol\";\nimport {StETHMock} from \"../contracts/mock/tokens/StETHMock.sol\";\nimport {MOR} from \"../contracts/old/MOR.sol\";\nimport {UniswapSwapRouterMock} from \"../contracts/mock/capital-protocol/uniswap/UniswapSwapRouterMock.sol\";\nimport {\n    IL2TokenReceiverV2,\n    IERC165,\n    IERC721Receiver\n} from \"../contracts/interfaces/capital-protocol/IL2TokenReceiverV2.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC1967Proxy} from \"../lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol\";\n\ncontract L2TokenReceiverV2Test is Test {\n    L2TokenReceiverV2 public l2TokenReceiver;\n    NonfungiblePositionManagerMock public nftManager;\n    UniswapSwapRouterMock public swapRouter;\n    StETHMock public inputToken;\n    MOR public outputToken;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        // Deploy mocks\n        inputToken = new StETHMock();\n        outputToken = new MOR(1);\n        swapRouter = new UniswapSwapRouterMock();\n        nftManager = new NonfungiblePositionManagerMock();\n\n        // Deploy implementation\n        L2TokenReceiverV2 impl = new L2TokenReceiverV2();\n\n        // Deploy proxy with initializer call\n        ERC1967Proxy proxy = new ERC1967Proxy(\n            address(impl),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(\n                L2TokenReceiverV2.L2TokenReceiver__init.selector,\n                address(swapRouter),\n                address(nftManager),\n                IL2TokenReceiverV2.SwapParams({\n                    tokenIn: address(inputToken),\n                    tokenOut: address(outputToken),\n                    fee: 500,\n                    sqrtPriceLimitX96: 0\n                })\n            )\n        );\n\n        // Cast proxy to L2TokenReceiverV2\n        l2TokenReceiver = L2TokenReceiverV2(address(proxy));\n    }\n\n    function test_increaseLiquidityCurrentRange_usesBlockTimestampAsDeadline() public {\n        // Mint a mock NFT to the L2TokenReceiver contract\n        uint256 tokenId = nftManager.mint(address(l2TokenReceiver));\n\n        uint256 tsBefore = block.timestamp;\n\n        // Make the call as the owner\n        vm.prank(l2TokenReceiver.owner());\n        l2TokenReceiver.increaseLiquidityCurrentRange(tokenId, 1 ether, 0, 0, 0);\n\n        uint256 lastDeadline = nftManager.lastDeadline();\n\n        assertEq(lastDeadline, tsBefore, \"Deadline should equal block.timestamp\");\n        vm.warp(100);\n        tsBefore = block.timestamp;\n        vm.prank(l2TokenReceiver.owner());\n        l2TokenReceiver.increaseLiquidityCurrentRange(tokenId, 1 ether, 0, 0, 0);\n\n        lastDeadline = nftManager.lastDeadline();\n\n        assertEq(lastDeadline, tsBefore, \"Deadline should equal block.timestamp\");\n    }\n}\n\ncontract NonfungiblePositionManagerMock {\n    uint256 public lastDeadline;\n    uint256 public nextTokenId = 1;\n    mapping(uint256 => address) public ownerOf;\n\n    function mint(address to) external returns (uint256 tokenId) {\n        tokenId = nextTokenId++;\n        ownerOf[tokenId] = to;\n    }\n\n    function increaseLiquidity(INonfungiblePositionManager.IncreaseLiquidityParams calldata params)\n        external\n        payable\n        returns (uint128 liquidity, uint256 amount0, uint256 amount1)\n    {\n        lastDeadline = params.deadline;\n        liquidity = uint128(params.amount0Desired + params.amount1Desired);\n        amount0 = params.amount0Desired;\n        amount1 = params.amount1Desired;\n    }\n\n    function positions(uint256)\n        external\n        pure\n        returns (uint96, address, address, address, uint24, int24, int24, uint128, uint256, uint256, uint128, uint128)\n    {}\n}\n```",
